            <ArticleTitle>Inflammatory fibroid polyp or Vanek's tumour.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 65-year-old woman who presented with recurrent episodes of severe, postprandial abdominal pain followed by projectile vomiting. Gastroscopy revealed a large polyp in the prepyloric region. During peristalsis, the polyp was repeatedly 'passing' through the pylorus into the duodenal bulb, hence obstructing the lumen. The polyp was eventually removed in a piecemeal fashion. Histopathologic examination revealed an inflammatory fibroid polyp (known also as Vanek's tumour). A brief review on inflammatory fibroid polyps follows.</AbstractText>
